// LexRules grammar-as-data (T-6 / B2-OMNI): `LexRules` is a `Node`. The tokenizer
// recognizes rules by structural shape (NodeKind, Connective, EdgeDiscipline on
// children) — never by ad-hoc `Symbol` spellings inside the generic stage.
// Wave-1 E0 void lex: canonical empty rule-book = `TypeNode { connective: Conj }`
// with `children == []` (`is_empty_conj_root` on the root). Future lexical rows
// attach as `EdgeLabel.Named` fields under a Conj root; until the lexical walk is
// realized, any non-empty Conj root closes as `Outcome::Rejected` with
// `tokenize_lexical_walk_not_realized` (fail-closed — no partial TokenStream).
